; Keil refuses arithmetic on a type operator applied to a label that is
; defined further down: + and - give A61, other operators A63. A comparison
; is fine if the other side refers to a later symbol too. Arithmetic inside
; the operand is fine, and parentheses around the operator do not help.
$MOD167
Prg     SECTION CODE
Main    PROC    NEAR
        JMP     FAR Later + 2
        JMP     SHORT Later - 2
        CALL    NEAR PTR Later + 0
        DW      Later - FAR Later
        DW      (NEAR Later) + 2
        DW      FAR (Later + 2) + 2
        DW      FAR Later * 2
        DW      WORD Later OR 1
        DW      2 SHL BYTE Later
        DW      FAR Later LT Later
        DW      FAR (Later + 2)
        DW      HIGH FAR Later
        JMP     FAR Later
        JMP     SHORT cc_Z, Later
        JMP     NEAR cc_Z, Later
        CALL    FAR [R2]
        JMP     cc_Z, SHORT [R2]
        JMP     WORD PTR [R3]
Later:  RET
Main    ENDP
Prg     ENDS

Abs     SECTION CODE AT 0D000H
Ap      PROC    NEAR
Back:   NOP
        DW      FAR Back + 2
        DW      DWORD Fwd SHR 1
        DW      FAR Fwd - Fwd
        DW      BYTE Fwd AND 0FFH
        DW      2 + SHORT Fwd
        DW      FAR Fwd GE Back
        DW      FAR Fwd LT Fwd
        DW      FAR Fwd EQ Fwd2
        DW      Fwd EQ FAR Fwd
        DW      5 NE NEAR Fwd
        DW      FAR Back EQ Fwd
        JMP     FAR Fwd + 0
Fwd:    RET
Fwd2:   RET
Ap      ENDP
Abs     ENDS
        END
